.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt LIBSYSCTLCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sysctlcmp_client_open ,
.Nm sysctlcmp_client_close ,
.Nm sysctlcmp_get ,
.Nm sysctlcmp_set ,
.Nm sysctlcmp_oidfmt ,
.Nm sysctlcmp_describe ,
.Nm sysctlcmp_next
.Nd client interface to the system.Sysctl capability
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libsysctlcmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sysctlcmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn sysctlcmp_client_open "struct sysctlcmp_client **clientp"
.Ft void
.Fn sysctlcmp_client_close "struct sysctlcmp_client *client"
.Ft int
.Fn sysctlcmp_get "struct sysctlcmp_client *client" "const char *name" "void *buf" "size_t *lenp"
.Ft int
.Fn sysctlcmp_set "struct sysctlcmp_client *client" "const char *name" "const void *value" "size_t len"
.Ft int
.Fn sysctlcmp_oidfmt "struct sysctlcmp_client *client" "const char *name" "unsigned int *kindp" "char *fmt" "size_t *fmtlenp"
.Ft int
.Fn sysctlcmp_describe "struct sysctlcmp_client *client" "const char *name" "char *buf" "size_t *lenp"
.Ft int
.Fn sysctlcmp_next "struct sysctlcmp_client *client" "const char *name" "char *buf" "size_t *lenp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions read and write kernel
.Xr sysctl 3
variables by name through the
.Dq system.Sysctl
capability rather than by calling
.Xr sysctl 3
directly, so a capability-mode program obtains sysctl access as a held
capability, subject to the provider's per-label policy.
.Pp
.Fn sysctlcmp_client_open
acquires the capability over the process's lookup channel.
.Fn sysctlcmp_get
reads
.Fa name
into
.Fa buf ;
.Fa *lenp
is the buffer size on entry and the value length on return.
If the buffer is too small the call fails with
.Er ENOMEM
and
.Fa *lenp
holds the required size.
.Fn sysctlcmp_set
writes
.Fa value
to
.Fa name ,
which the provider permits only when the caller's label is authorized to write
that variable.
.Pp
.Fn sysctlcmp_oidfmt
returns the sysctl kind in
.Fa *kindp
and its NUL-terminated format string in
.Fa fmt .
.Fn sysctlcmp_describe
returns the NUL-terminated description of
.Fa name .
For both calls, the associated length argument is the buffer size on entry and
receives the returned size, including the terminating NUL.
.Fn sysctlcmp_next
returns the next policy-visible sysctl name after
.Fa name ;
an empty or NULL name starts enumeration and
.Er ENOENT
marks its end.
The returned name is NUL-terminated.
Malformed string replies fail with
.Er EPROTO
and invalidate the session.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std sysctlcmp_client_open sysctlcmp_get sysctlcmp_set sysctlcmp_oidfmt sysctlcmp_describe sysctlcmp_next
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 3 ,
.Xr localsysctl 8
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Read and write access is scoped per label by the provider; a variable not
named in the caller's allow-list is refused with
.Er EPERM ,
and writes are denied by default.
